{"id": "EUVD-2026-64377", "enisaUuid": "ea4cb33b-8d30-3b9c-b08b-b59e254e6bd1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/ism: Fix UAF of sba and ieq during ism_dev_exit()\n\nA ism interrupt handler can be active in parallel with ism_dev_exit(),\naccessing freed data structures.\n\nNo new interrupts will be generated after unregister_ieq(). Drain ongoing\ninterrupt handlers by free_irq(), before freeing ism data structures.", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:32:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:09", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/950dac9e8c4e3cf68fa8c01f77d3ac3b7369c6a9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58803870ba0841e53b630a1290c6838b091dd128", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc3021284050ecb3bba8a7851340cedcb5037928", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/774394d27930ec4cf4cb3eed8ab6a4d20cb2430a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b1896543ce59c4258625a35cf41e23a9a1f80ea2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f2p8-hwvr-fwmq", "CVE-2026-74690"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09a95547-38a2-383a-a42b-82e3fe5c5ad4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "684b89bc39ce4f204b1a2b180f39f2eb36a6b695 <950dac9e8c4e3cf68fa8c01f77d3ac3b7369c6a9"}, {"id": "4e11b5c1-201c-3dd4-9dc3-fca4167db48b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.45"}, {"id": "51f87436-f437-3f02-8e4b-07ba2acc2d51", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6a798149-56e3-3d35-b3d1-aa5459e2eb61", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "684b89bc39ce4f204b1a2b180f39f2eb36a6b695 <b1896543ce59c4258625a35cf41e23a9a1f80ea2"}, {"id": "78e2c75e-960d-3990-b33c-f90cfba2a644", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version